emote branches). Design rev9 §5.6 *does* fully specify a schema for it (`transaction_id, tool_call_id, session_id, turn_index, query_hash, limit, result_status, returned[]{rank, stable_id, revision, content_hash, score?}`) that was apparently never implemented. Since rev10 doesn't redefine the event, only assumes and extends it, I did not treat this as a hard blocker — I built `memory.search_result` now, modeling its shape on X3's fully-specified `graphiti.search_result` (`tool_call_id, query_sha256, rewritten_query_sha256, rewrite_status, returned[]{stable_id, content_sha256}, result_status`) rather than rev9's older field names (no `rank`/`limit`/`revision`/`content_hash`/explicit `transaction_id`/`turn_index` in `data`), since X3 is the concrete template this task handed me and the \"关键断言\" list only tests `result_status`/`rewrite_status`/`rewritten_query_sha256`. Flagging this explicitly since it's a real design-vs-code gap, not something I should have silently resolved.\n2. `reference_time_source` enum values (`\"entry_timestamp\"`, `\"message_timestamp_epoch\"`, `\"none\"`) are my own naming — the plan only pins down `\"none\"` explicitly.\n3. Pre-existing test files (`graphiti-auto-sync.test.ts`, `graphiti-tool.test.ts`, `memory-search-tool.test.ts`) now trigger `getWriter().emit()` for the first time via my production-code changes. Since the observability writer defaults to `~/.pi/agent/observability` when unset, I added `MA_OBS_DIR`-temp-dir + `resetWriterForTests()` sandboxing to these files (matching the existing convention in `tests/observability/memory-events.test.ts`) so `npm test` never writes outside the temp dirs.\n4. `node_modules` is a symlink (`node_modules -&gt; /Users/youxun/pi-hermes-memory-wt-slice1/node_modules`) I created per setup instructions. `.gitignore` has `node_modules/` (directory-only pattern), which does **not** match a symlink — `git check-ignore -v node_modules` confirms it is NOT ignored. I did not stage it (`git add` listed exact files only); `git status --short` after commit shows only `?? node_modules`.\n\n### Uncertain / worth a second look\n- `result_status` for `memory_search`/`memory.search_result` only has `ok`/`empty` — I didn't invent an `error` path since the existing `memory_search` code has no caught-error branch to hang one off; X4's key assertion only required `empty`.\n- `graphiti.search_result`'s `result_status:\"error\"` is keyed off `!result.success` (both `search_memory_facts` and `search_nodes` failing) per the spec text \"调用出错为 error\"; a facts-only success with nodes-only failure still reports `ok`/`empty` based on fact count, which I believe matches the spec's fact-centric framing but isn't explicitly pinned down there.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>367614</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>71</tool_uses><duration_ms>843653</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5046822e6ca46f13</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011Pu1fUB1F84L7fJk99Jm2T</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-agent-eval/07ac599c-2761-4651-b18d-ea374efd5f2b/tasks/a5046822e6ca46f13.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"T-RN generic harness runner\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Committed cleanly, `git status --short` is empty. Here's the final report for this fix.\n\n## Fix report — group-atomic resume\n\n**Commit:** `54d29a5 fix(harness): group-atomic resume` (on top of `727233c`)\n**Worktree:** `/Users/youxun/project/agent-eval/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5046822e6ca46f13`\n**Branch:** `worktree-agent-a5046822e6ca46f13`\n**`git status --short`:** clean\n\n### Diff summary\n`src/harness/run-case-group.ts` (+154/-42 relative to prior commit):\n- New pure helpers: `groupAttempt(records)` (max attempt across whatever exists, 0 if none), `isGroupTerminal(records)` (all completed, or `groupAttempt &gt;= 2`), `supersedeGroup(evidenceDir, recordPaths, existingRecords)` (moves existing record files + the previous `run-ledger.json`, if any, into `superseded/&lt;ISO-timestamp&gt;/`; no-op on a first run).\n- `runCaseGroup` now reads all existing repeat records up front, before calling anything on `target`. If `isGroupTerminal`, it returns those records verbatim and exits — `prepare`/`ingest`/`quiesce`/`export_baseline`/`freeze`/`query`/`dispose` are never called. Otherwise it computes one group-level `attempt`, calls `prepare`, supersedes old files, and reruns the whole group (setup once, all repeats fresh) on the single new baseline.\n- `runOneRepeat` no longer reads/skips per-repeat; it takes `path` and `attempt` as plain parameters. `RepeatOutcome` dropped its now-always-true `ran` field.\n- The setup-failure branch writes a failed record for every repeat at the group's `attempt`, with no per-repeat skip.\n- `shouldSkipRepeat` import removed from this file (function itself untouched in `records-io.ts`; its own tests still pass).\n\n`src/harness/run-case-group.test.ts` (+155/-0 net): 4 new tests, all 9 pre-existing tests unmodified and passing.\n\n### `pnpm check` tail (verbatim)\n```\n[4] 守卫的变异测试 —— 证明它们不是空转\n   ✓ 越界抽取被挡住（exit=1）\n   ✓ 小节缺失被挡住（exit=1）\nmake-dispatch-prompt：全部通过\n   ✓\n\n结果：全部通过。\n```\nExit code 0. Grep gate (`grep -rniE 'hermes|graphiti|neo4j|sqlite|\\bpi\\b' src/harness --include='*.ts' | grep -vE '\\.test\\.ts|fake-target\\.ts'`) → empty.\n\n### New test names\n- `全部 repeat 都已终结（completed）时，resume 不调用任何 target 方法`\n- `组内已有一条 attempt=2 的失败记录（重试上限已用完）时，即便其余 repeat 已完成也不再重跑`\n- `部分完成的组整组重跑：只有一次 ingest，三个 repeat 共享同一个新 baseline，旧记录移入 superseded/`\n- `attempt 计数：已有记录的最大 attempt 为 1 时，整组重跑后的新 attempt 为 2`\n\n### Mutation results\n- **(a) reintroduced per-repeat skip** for already-completed repeats inside the rerun branch → `部分完成的组整组重跑…` failed with `all three